 "whisper_heard": {
  "s1": "A grain of sand is about half a millimetre. A human hair is a tenth of that. And that's about where your eyes give up.",
  "s2": "A red blood cell is ten times smaller again. Most viruses are smaller still, too small for any ordinary microscope to see.",
  "s3": "An atom is a thousand times smaller than a virus. And the proton at its centre is sixty thousand times smaller than the atom.",
  "s4": "Electrons are so small that no experiment has found any size at all. Below that, physicists point to the Planck length, twenty more zeros down.",
  "s5": "Thirty -four zeros after the decimal point. Maybe that's the floor. Or maybe there isn't one."
